## 1. Basic Calculator (Switch Case)
 Using `switch` to create a menu-driven program for arithmetic operations. This is more efficient than a long chain of `if-else` statements for simple menu selection.

### Java Implementation:
```java
int n = sc.nextInt(); // Operator Choice (1-4)
int a = sc.nextInt(); // First Number
int b = sc.nextInt(); // Second Number

switch(n) {
    case 1: 
        System.out.println(a + b); 
        break;
    case 2: 
        System.out.println(a - b); 
        break;
    case 3: 
        System.out.println(a * b); 
        break;
    case 4: 
        if (b != 0) {
            System.out.println(a / b);
        } else {
            System.out.println("Error: Division by zero");
        }
        break;
    default: 
        System.out.println("Give numbers between 1-4");
}
```

