## 4. Complex Character Math: Reverse Position Weighting
**The Challenge:** Calculate a sum where each character is mapped to its mirrored alphabetical position ($a=26, b=25...z=1$) and multiplied by its 1-based index in the string.

### Calculation Logic for "abc":
| Character | Reverse Value ($26 - (ch - 'a')$) | Position (i + 1) | Product |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **a** | 26 | 1 | $26 \times 1 = 26$ |
| **b** | 25 | 2 | $25 \times 2 = 50$ |
| **c** | 24 | 3 | $24 \times 3 = 72$ |
| **Final Output** | | | **148** |

### Code Implementation:
```java
int sum = 0;
for(int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {
    int reverseVal = 26 - (s.charAt(i) - 'a');
    sum += reverseVal * (i + 1);
}
System.out.println(sum);
